## Merge Checklist — tools/ directory

When merging feature branches into main (or vice versa), verify:

```bash
# 1. Check if any tools/ files have merge conflicts
git diff --name-only --diff-filter=U | grep "^tools/"

# 2. Verify Tier 1 tools are present after merge
ls tools/hybrid_flow.py tools/check_merge_readiness.py tools/test_handoff_gui.pyw tools/prompt_generator_gui.py

# 3. Check if newer tools exist in feature branch but not in main
git log --oneline --diff-filter=A -- tools/  # shows Add commits
```

**Conflict resolution priority**:
- `hybrid_flow.py`, `hybrid_flow-tasks.json` → Keep **feature branch** version (newer features)
- `check_merge_readiness.py` → Keep **main** version (stricter checks preferred)
- New tools added in feature branch → **Always keep** (don't discard)

---

## Why This File Exists

During merges, git merges file content automatically but:
1. New files added in feature branches may not conflict but can be overlooked in `--no-ff` squash merges
2. Deleted files in either branch will be removed by git
3. This file serves as a human checklist for post-merge verification

